  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Brazier of Holy Fire" id="3ac9-d1fa-175c-9511" hidden="false" page="44" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Any model hit in close combat is set on fire on a 4+ (as per the Flamer entry).
Once per game can shoot the Brazier as if it were a Heavy Flamer. Can move and fire unlike a regular heavy flamer</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Flail of Chastisement" id="ee16-4433-c3f2-dbe3" hidden="false" page="44" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>If a target is wounded by the Flail but not killed, it loses D3 Attacks in the next round of combat reducing its Attacks to a minimum of 1</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Veteran Superior" id="60bf-1736-b0b1-4b11" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Before the game, the Veteran Superior may lead her squad in one of the Sacred Rites. As a Veteran Superior, she adds +2 to the roll.

May fire two pistols in the shooting phase, with a -1 to hit for each shot. These can be targeted against the same or different targets.

A Seraphim armed with two hand flamers may fire them in combination, using them with the regular Flamer stats instead of a hand flamer</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Canoness" id="9ee1-6026-c4f9-30e2" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Before the game, the Canoness may lead her squad in one of the Sacred Rites. She adds +3 to the roll.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Banner Bearer" id="9691-8071-67d6-94dd" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Must stay within 2&quot; squad coherency of the Canoness or her Bodyguard for the duration of the battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Training of the Order" id="0cce-31d6-9a3e-0d41" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>May fire two pistols in the shooting phase, with a -1 to hit for each shot. These can be targeted against the same or different targets.

If armed with two hand flamers may fire them in combination, using them with the regular Flamer stats instead of a hand flamer</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Missionary Rite" id="888f-6a5f-09b0-4a13" hidden="false" page="55" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>A squad led by a Missionary at the start of the battle may perform a Sacred Rite.

A Missionary Mighty Hero allows you to add +1 to the roll</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Confessor" id="9f5f-f1d4-8840-cd24" hidden="false" page="55" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Subject to Frenzy
Never breaks and is immune to all other psychological effects

A squad led by a Confessor is subject to the rules for Frenzy and also never breaks and is immune to all other psychological effects

A Confessor and the sqaud he leads cannot test to restrain Frenzy</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Preacher" id="f7c2-4c73-81d4-0714" hidden="false" page="56" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>A squad led by a Preacher ma perform a Sacred Rite before the battle. A Preacher confers no bonus to the roll</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sister Superior" id="bb94-3bc7-53b5-1aec" hidden="false" page="57" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>May lead the squad in the Sacred Rites adding +1 to the roll</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rhino Damage Table" id="8927-60a1-34f2-aec3" hidden="false" page="Datafax">
      <description>1: Track - Closest track to shooter
2-5: Hull
6: Weapons
See datafax for damage table</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Immolator Damage Table" id="a64d-ad95-21e9-c18f" hidden="false" page="Datafax" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>1: Track - Closest track to shooter
2-4: Hull
5-6: Weapons - On side/read, roll again. 1-3, Turret hit, 4-6, Gunner hit
See datafax for damage table and Sisters Codex pg. 47 for Turret rules in damage</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Twin Heavy Flamer" id="2a77-b3fa-24c9-533b" hidden="false" page="46" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>The Immolator&apos;s twin flamers must fire together either as a focused blast or in a wide spread. 
Focused blast you place the Heavy Flamer template as normal and every model under takes 2 hits. Any partial models, roll a 4+ to see if they are also hit (and taking two wounds).  This also causes 2 fire tests to see if the model is lit on fire. 
If firing the wide spread, place 2 heavy flamer templates side by side. Models that are partially under both templates count as hit (consider the 2 templates as 1 large one). Any that are partial on the edge like normal roll a 4+ to see if hit. 

See Codex Sisters of Battle for further fire test rules pg. 47</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Praxedes Sacred Rites" id="8258-dc2e-7150-2e08" hidden="false" page="60" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Saint Praxedes may lead a squad in one of the Sacred Rites. As a Canoness she adds +3 to the roll</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Irresistible Charge" id="1b0a-cc86-7988-f49b" hidden="false" page="62" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>When Saint Praxedes charges an enemy in close combat roll a D6 and add her Strength. If the total is greater than the Strength of her opponent they are knocked off balance and must halve their Weapon Skill for the rest of the turn (rounding up)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Inspirational Leader" id="16fe-3dfc-865c-5035" hidden="false" page="62" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Any friendly troops with a line of sight to Saint Praxedes may add +1 to their Leadership for psychology and BReak tests. If Saint PRaxedes is fighting in close combat any squads or models with a line of sight to her may use her Leadership value of 10 for all psychology and Break tests. 
Any unit led by Saint PRaxedes adds +1 to its Weapon Skill if they charge the enemy in close combat</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Helena Sacred Rites" id="9fa8-0eca-d29f-10a9" hidden="false" page="60" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Helena may lead a squad in one of the Sacred Rites. She adds +4 to the roll. If the result is a 10, you may roll twice and apply both results to the squad. Re-roll any subsequent 10 or duplicate results

Every other squad in the army receives a bonus of +1 to its Sacred Rites rolls, which is in addition to any bonuses the character may add. If this takes the result to 10 or more, treat this as a roll of 9</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Holy Radiance" id="0f64-6a78-d3f2-662e" hidden="false" page="61" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Any fleeing Imperial squad within 12&quot; of Helena at the start of the rally phase automatically rallies. In addition, all troops with a line of sight to HElena may user her LEadership value of 10, not just those within 12&quot;.

Helena herself is completely immune to psychology and Break tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Revered Leader" id="84b4-a4e6-b5f6-fad4" hidden="false" page="61" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>If HElena is wounded all the troops in the army become subject to the rules for Hatred as detailed in the 40k Rulebook. If Helena should be killed, every squad that passes the subsequent Leadership test for the loss of their commander becomes ummune to Break tests for the rest of the battle.

If she is killed the enemy gains +5 Victory Points</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Uriah Sacred Rites" id="ae2a-d59f-3558-bd2f" hidden="false" page="62" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Jacobus may lead a squad in one of the Sacred Rites. As he has Litanies of Faith, you may roll two dice and choose which result applies. As a Missionary Mighty Hero Jacobus adds +1 to the roll</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Steadfast" id="ea2d-3872-388f-c958" hidden="false" page="62" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Jacobus absolutely will not give up or surrender. He is therefor immune to psychology and Break tests. If a squad he is with flees for any reason, Jacobus does not flee with them but remains where he is.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Helfire Sacred Rites" id="9994-dc74-3412-1652" hidden="false" page="64" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>May lead a squad in one of the Sacred Rites. +1 bonus to the roll</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Holy Disdain" id="741e-867c-9b65-8c2f" hidden="false" page="64" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Armandus is totally immune to Fear and Terror tests and cannot be broken. Should a squad accompanied by Armandus flee, he will remain in place and become separated from the unit</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Commanding Voice" id="accc-d695-bbcd-1c5e" hidden="false" page="64" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>If Armandus is the army commander, units within 18&quot; may use his Leadership of 10 rather than just units within 12&quot;</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ol&apos; Stony" id="a26f-1c35-190d-461d" hidden="false" page="64" publicationId="cad3-a694-b720-6309">
      <description>Any weapon that causes multiple damage which hits Armandus halves the number of wounds it inflicts (round fractions down, to a minimum of 1)</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
